tribution-module__TWKVxa__copy"><h3 class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__title type-h1">RESEARCH</h3><p class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__subtitle type-subtitle">Competitive Research</p><p class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__description type-body">Researched and analyzed comparable cases across large organizations and public-facing platforms to identify relevant approaches and references for the project.</p></div></div><div class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__area"><span class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__index type-display" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__copy"><h3 class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__title type-h1">STRUCTURE</h3><p class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__subtitle type-subtitle">Information Mapping &amp; Visualization</p><p class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__description type-body">Worked with the team lead to organize key information synthesized from client meeting recordings, then translated it into visual diagrams and maps to make complex relationships and service information easier to understand.</p></div></div><div class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__area"><span class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__index type-display" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__copy"><h3 class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__title type-h1">COMMUNICATION</h3><p class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__subtitle type-subtitle">Presentation Support</p><p class="contribution-module__TWKVxa__description type-body">Supported the final presentation preparation by explaining the diagrams and information structures I developed, answering team questions, and providing feedback as the presentation was refined.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__reflection" aria-labelledby="reflection-heading"><h2 id="reflection-heading" class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__label type-micro"><span>05</span><span>REFLECTION</span></h2><div class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__chapters"><article class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__chapter" aria-labelledby="reflection-01"><h3 id="reflection-01" class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__statement type-display">FINDING CLARITY IN COMPLEXITY.</h3><div class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__copy type-body"><p data-paragraph="true">This was my first UX and service design project, and the pace was very different from the interior design projects I was used to. Our team of more than 20 people had to quickly explore different directions, gather information from dozens of sources, and bring everything back together within a very short timeframe.</p><p data-paragraph="true">At first, I found it difficult to adapt to the amount and speed of information. Over time, however, this became one of the most rewarding parts of the project. I learned how to sort through scattered information, identify what was useful, decide what needed deeper exploration, and translate complex relationships into clear visual structures.</p><p data-paragraph="true">What I enjoyed most was finding clarity within complexity — looking at many disconnected pieces and gradually finding the most logical and effective way forward. It made me realize that, regardless of the medium, this is also what I value about design itself.</p></div><div class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__study" tabindex="0" role="img" aria-label="Scattered information organizes into aligned fragments on hover or focus."><svg viewBox="0 0 320 280" aria-hidden="true"><g class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__fragment" style="--start-x:30px;--start-y:30px;--end-x:56px;--end-y:52px;--fragment-opacity:0.32"><line x1="-7" y1="0" x2="7" y2="0"></line></g><g class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__fragment" style="--start-x:98px;--start-y:46px;--end-x:126px;--end-y:52px;--fragment-opacity:0.32"><line x1="-10" y1="0" x2="10" y2="0"></line></g><g class="reflection-module__4y0ywa__fragment" style="--start-x:166px;--start-y:24px;--end-x:196px;--end-y:52px;--fragment-opacity:0.32"><line x1="-8" y1="0" x2="8" y2="0"></line></g><g cla